Well, I heard there was a bomb on the bus, but I haven't had a chance to check it out.

00:07:13.730 --> 00:07:16.730
Even the dress shirt can't hide the heroin, you, huh, Claire?

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:17.730
A heck of a first day at the office.

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:20.730
Well, that's where I'm there, so I can be around to help more people.

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:23.730
Working in the Daily Planet, I'll hear about every crisis as it happens.

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:25.730
I just wish that you were there with me.

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:27.730
You know, now that Lex is in my.

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:29.730
Now that Lex isn't running things.

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:33.730
Yeah, I've spent almost my entire life praying to the gods of journalism.

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:35.730
It might be kind of nice to try something new, you know?

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:37.730
See how it feels?

00:07:37.730 --> 00:07:41.100
Now you're ready for a change?

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:45.100
Actually, uh, pretty big changes.

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:50.100
Apparently, the goddess of journalism is wondering where I am.

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:54.100
With Lois on the case, it's gonna get harder to duck away to save the day.

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:58.100
If I could hide my secret from you, I think I can handle your cousin.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:07:59.100
Good luck with that.

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:01.100
I gotta go.

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:05.100
Uh, tell Lois that I said to take it easy on you.

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:19.839
Whoa, Clark, what happened? Are you okay?

00:08:19.839 --> 00:08:21.839
