00:08:21.839 --> 00:08:24.839
Oh, no. I'm trying to chase down a lead on this story.

00:08:24.839 --> 00:08:27.839
I don't want to have to chase after you, too.

00:08:27.839 --> 00:08:30.839
Hey, did you happen to hear anything while you were out there making your ash angels?

00:08:30.839 --> 00:08:32.840
Actually, I did.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:34.840
The police think the bomb misfired since there weren't any casualties.

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:36.840
I don't feel like a misfired to me.

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:39.840
All right? Who's your source?

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:42.340
Who's your source?

00:08:42.340 --> 00:08:43.340
I'm sorry, Lois. I didn't you.

00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:46.340
get a name. I was too busy, you know, helping people.

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:51.340
Okay. Rule number one? Always know your source.

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:57.340
I understand. Look, if you're gonna teach a class on Lois Lane's rules of reporting,

00:08:57.340 --> 00:08:59.340
I think I'd rather read the Cliff Notes.

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:01.340
Boss wants to see you now.

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:06.389
Okay, my first official meeting with our latest leader.

00:09:06.389 --> 00:09:08.389
Not you. Can't.

00:09:08.389 --> 00:09:12.389
Oh. Well, you're gonna want to clean yourself up.

00:09:12.389 --> 00:09:15.370
Rule number two, always make a good first and first and

00:09:15.389 --> 00:09:17.389
and don't screw up with the boss.

00:09:17.389 --> 00:09:19.389
I think that's two rules.

00:09:19.389 --> 00:09:23.389
Whatever. Try not to get fired on your first day, okay?

00:09:23.389 --> 00:09:43.539
Have a seat, Mr. Kent.

00:09:43.539 --> 00:09:57.320
Test Mercer, acting CEO of Luther Corps.

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:59.320
You're my boss?

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:02.320
You weren't the shy when I was the damsel in distress, Kent.

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:05.320
Don't tell me you're intimidated by a powerful woman.

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:08.320
No, I just... I'm surprised to see you back at work so soon.

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:10.320
Oh, I have big shoes to fill.

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:12.320
And the paramedics said that I was fine.

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:14.730
It's unusual, isn't it?

00:10:14.730 --> 00:10:15.730
The news.

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:18.730
CEO of Luther Corp be taking the bus to work?

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:19.730
I'm going green.

00:10:19.730 --> 00:10:22.730
You know, doing what I can to save the planet.

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:25.730
But for the sake of the shareholders, let's keep that between ourselves.

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:29.730
Seems we were destined to meet.

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:37.340
I already had you on my to-do list today.

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:39.340
Lex told me all about you.

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:44.779
Not much to tell, really.

00:10:44.779 --> 00:10:49.610
He said you have a thing for saving people.

00:10:49.610 --> 00:10:52.610
And after this morning, I'd say that's true.

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:56.610
Ever since Lex's disappearance, I have used all of Luther Corp's

00:10:56.610 --> 00:10:57.610
resources to find him.

00:10:57.610 --> 00:10:58.610
Do you have any leads?

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:00.610
The world's a big place.

00:11:00.610 --> 00:11:04.610
