The police say there's no evidence of a bomb.

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:55.710
I think someone with a meteor power may have caused a blast.

00:17:55.710 --> 00:18:01.839
What's a meteor power?

00:18:01.839 --> 00:18:07.839
Sometimes people develop special abilities after being exposed to a certain type of meteor rock.

00:18:07.839 --> 00:18:09.839
Tommy.

00:18:09.839 --> 00:18:11.839
Another street kid.

00:18:11.839 --> 00:18:17.839
He told me he found this weird rock a couple days ago, and now whenever he gets angry, things heat up.

00:18:17.839 --> 00:18:20.839
I thought he was messing with me.

00:18:20.839 --> 00:18:21.839
We got no fight today.

00:18:21.839 --> 00:18:24.839
He was being a jerk, so I ran onto the bus to get away from him.

00:18:24.839 --> 00:18:26.839
Do you know where I can find him?

00:18:26.839 --> 00:18:28.839
I know where he hangs. I think I can remember how to get there.

00:18:28.839 --> 00:18:30.839
Wait, but this guy sounds dangerous.

00:18:30.839 --> 00:18:32.839
I don't think you should go.

00:18:32.839 --> 00:18:34.839
I'll wait in the car. I can point him out to you.

00:18:34.839 --> 00:18:46.890
There, sitting down.

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:50.460
I saw him earlier.

00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:51.460
He was running away from the bus.

00:18:51.460 --> 00:19:02.420
It's all right. I just want to talk.

00:19:02.420 --> 00:19:08.420
Tommy, it's okay.

00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:09.420
Stay here.

00:19:09.420 --> 00:19:13.299
Tommy!

00:19:13.299 --> 00:19:17.460
Get away from me!

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:18.460
Get away from me!

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:21.460
It'll be okay, Tommy. I promise.

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:23.460
No, no, no, you're lying!

00:19:23.460 --> 00:19:24.460
Well, just be calm, all right?

00:19:24.460 --> 00:19:25.460
There's no reason for anyone to get hurt.

00:19:25.460 --> 00:19:27.460
Get away from me!

00:19:27.460 --> 00:19:29.460
Bet, stay back. You could be dangerous.

00:19:29.460 --> 00:19:32.460
How could you do this to me?

00:19:32.460 --> 00:19:35.460
Just... just stay away!

00:19:35.460 --> 00:19:59.799
You're scared, Lois.

00:19:59.799 --> 00:20:02.799
I don't think he meant to hurt anyone. He just couldn't control his powers.

00:20:02.799 --> 00:20:04.799
He blew up a bus, Clark.

00:20:04.799 --> 00:20:05.799
Almost killed a lot of people.

00:20:05.799 --> 00:20:07.799
I'd say this was textbook karma.

00:20:07.799 --> 00:20:12.450
Thanks.

00:20:12.450 --> 00:20:13.450
Hey, you didn't tell me that you were wrong.

00:20:13.450 --> 00:20:15.289
Tell me that you were recording that.

00:20:15.289 --> 00:20:17.049
Don't get your tights in a twist, Smallville.

00:20:17.049 --> 00:20:19.410
I'll just refer to you as sources say.

00:20:19.410 --> 00:20:21.630
Besides, if I'm gonna write Tommy was a human bomb,

00:20:21.630 --> 00:20:24.170
I need scientific proof.

00:20:24.170 --> 00:20:25.769
We could check the autopsy report,

00:20:25.769 --> 00:20:27.589
see how much meteor rock was in his system.

00:20:27.589 --> 00:20:28.829
The coroner won't release it

00:20:28.829 --> 00:20:33.009
if it's part of an ongoing investigation.

00:20:33.009 --> 00:20:36.789
But I bet we could find a copy lying around the hospital.

00:20:36.789 --> 00:20:38.950
By fine, I'm assuming you mean steal.

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:42.170
Rule number three, do whatever it takes to get the story.

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:43.630
You really should be writing these down.

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:44.470
Always be careful.

00:20:44.470 --> 00:20:45.089
There's some lines you should.

00:20:45.109 --> 00:20:46.109
You shouldn't cross.

00:20:46.109 --> 00:20:49.109
The only line I'm worried about is a byline,

00:20:49.109 --> 00:20:51.109
and so should you, Clark, wearing this together.

00:20:51.109 --> 00:20:53.109
You want to share a byline with me?

00:20:53.109 --> 00:20:54.109
Oh, God, no.

00:20:54.109 --> 00:20:56.109
But I got you the obit.

00:20:56.109 --> 00:20:57.109
Tommy's obituary?

00:20:57.109 --> 00:20:58.109
Absolutely.

00:20:58.109 --> 00:21:01.109
You helped break the story, so you get to commemorate the kid

00:21:01.109 --> 00:21:03.109
in 10 lines or less.

00:21:03.109 --> 00:21:05.109
Don't be so squeamish.

00:21:05.109 --> 00:21:07.109
Most of us got started writing Wantats.

00:21:07.109 --> 00:21:08.109
You know what?

00:21:08.109 --> 00:21:10.109
There was a time when I would have killed for an obit.

00:21:10.109 --> 00:21:31.089
Are you coming?

00:21:31.089 --> 00:21:33.089
You know, if you just reach a little bit higher,

00:21:33.089 --> 00:21:35.089
you're definitely gonna need an ambulance.

00:21:35.089 --> 00:21:38.089
Yes, I'm lucky there's a paramedic in the building.

00:21:38.089 --> 00:21:46.700
Yeah, well, you asked me to bring her over this application.

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:49.230
Give me.

00:21:49.230 --> 00:21:55.230
Oh, I did talk to my friend, and she says that there's a spot open at the home for bed.

00:21:55.230 --> 00:21:57.640
That's great.

00:21:57.640 --> 00:22:04.450
She could really use some good news right now.

00:22:04.450 --> 00:22:09.450
Her day got even worse a little while ago, and she needed some space, so I came here.

00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:18.509
Alicia, you had a place to say it.

00:22:18.509 --> 00:22:19.509
Thanks to you.

00:22:19.509 --> 00:22:23.579
Thanks.

00:22:23.579 --> 00:22:29.319
Isis Foundation.

00:22:29.319 --> 00:22:31.319
foundation. So what? Adoptive a Pyramids,

00:22:31.319 --> 00:22:33.319
Ava Sphinx, that kind of thing?

00:22:33.319 --> 00:22:35.319
Cute.

00:22:35.319 --> 00:22:37.319
Uh, actually, it's more like a counselling center.

00:22:37.319 --> 00:22:39.319
I'm house-sitting for a friend of mine

00:22:39.319 --> 00:22:41.319
until she finds someone to take it over.

00:22:41.319 --> 00:22:44.319
I'm surprised I haven't heard of it. The hospital sends out updates

00:22:44.319 --> 00:22:46.319
on all the mental health facilities.

00:22:46.319 --> 00:22:48.319
Well, she has very specific clients.

00:22:48.319 --> 00:22:53.319
People with special skills that are sometimes a little dangerous.

00:22:53.319 --> 00:22:56.319
We mean like meteor types?

00:22:56.319 --> 00:22:58.319
Drive an ambulance in Metropolis, Chloe.

00:22:58.319 --> 00:23:00.319
is Chloe, I've seen a lot of things,

00:23:00.319 --> 00:23:05.980
at least enough to know that they could use the help.

00:23:05.980 --> 00:23:07.980
Have you ever thought about helping them?

00:23:07.980 --> 00:23:08.980
No, I don't.

00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:10.980
I saw you with Beth today.

00:23:10.980 --> 00:23:11.980
You carried enough to take her under your wing.

00:23:11.980 --> 00:23:13.980
That's rare.

00:23:13.980 --> 00:23:16.980
And think how hard it must be for these meteor people

00:23:16.980 --> 00:23:18.980
to find someone they can trust.

00:23:18.980 --> 00:23:20.980
But am I streetwise enough?

00:23:20.980 --> 00:23:23.980
Okay, forget what I said earlier.

00:23:23.980 --> 00:23:25.980
I can come off a little strong.

00:23:25.980 --> 00:23:29.980
It's okay. At least now I understand where it comes from.

00:23:29.980 --> 00:23:31.980
Understand how?

00:23:31.980 --> 00:23:33.980
Well, I googled you.

00:23:33.980 --> 00:23:35.980
And I read an interview that you gave

00:23:35.980 --> 00:23:37.980
about running away from foster homes as a kid.

00:23:37.980 --> 00:23:38.980
You researched me?

00:23:38.980 --> 00:23:43.609
Well, you know, I always kind of wanted my own stalker.

00:23:43.609 --> 00:23:45.609
It isn't like that, Davis.

00:23:45.609 --> 00:23:47.609
It's just that, no, really.

00:23:47.609 --> 00:23:49.609
I used to be a reporter, and so I have a serious

00:23:49.609 --> 00:23:52.609
curiosity complex.

00:23:52.609 --> 00:23:53.609
Okay, yeah.

00:23:53.609 --> 00:23:58.460
And I'm engaged.

00:23:58.460 --> 00:24:00.460
You're the first person I've told about that.

00:24:00.460 --> 00:24:02.460
Well, congratulations.

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:03.460
That's a very...

00:24:03.460 --> 00:24:05.460
A very unique engagement ring.

00:24:05.460 --> 00:24:10.460
Uh, well, you know, it's the story behind the ring that really makes it special.

00:24:10.460 --> 00:24:11.460
Hmm?

00:24:11.460 --> 00:24:17.079
I went away for a little while and he never gave up on me.

00:24:17.079 --> 00:24:23.079
Oh, Chloe, I grew up hearing a lot of four-letter words and love wasn't exactly one of them.

00:24:23.079 --> 00:24:28.420
If you found it, real love?

00:24:28.420 --> 00:24:29.420
Hold on to do it.

00:24:29.420 --> 00:25:13.170
And if anyone tells you that that's a cliche, I'll personally kick their ass.

00:25:13.170 --> 00:25:14.170
Did you find her?

00:25:14.170 --> 00:25:16.170
She's gone off the grid again.

00:25:16.170 --> 00:25:18.769
Don't come back.

00:25:18.769 --> 00:25:27.269
until you do. Is there something else?

00:25:27.269 --> 00:25:28.269
The girl's dangerous.

00:25:28.269 --> 00:25:31.269
You tried to approach her on the bus, and she blew it up.

00:25:31.269 --> 00:25:37.190
Mr. Luther would have had us terminate the problem on site.

00:25:37.190 --> 00:25:39.190
I'm your boss now.

00:25:39.190 --> 00:25:44.190
And since we've never worked together, I can't trust that you'll see this through to my satisfaction.

00:25:44.190 --> 00:25:47.190
Bring her here. I'll handle her.

00:25:47.190 --> 00:25:49.190
End of story.

00:25:49.190 --> 00:26:08.319
Law, she can't just walk in and steal a file.

00:26:08.319 --> 00:26:10.319
It's a crime. You'll go to prison.

00:26:10.319 --> 00:26:11.319
I have a plan, Clark.

00:26:11.319 --> 00:26:12.319
You'd like to share it.

00:26:12.319 --> 00:26:14.319
I'm having doubts.

00:26:14.319 --> 00:26:16.319
When in doubt?

00:26:16.319 --> 00:26:18.319
Charge it.

00:26:18.319 --> 00:26:21.319
City Hall, 13th, precinct, 15th, precinct.

00:26:21.319 --> 00:26:24.319
The Tropolis General.

00:26:24.319 --> 00:26:29.619
If I could just get mileage points on these things, I'd see the world.

00:26:29.619 --> 00:26:31.619
Cover me, small, well.

00:26:31.619 --> 00:26:45.950
Uh, you know, patients are on an entirely different floor.

00:26:45.950 --> 00:26:48.950
You know, I thought I got off the elevator a little early.

00:26:48.950 --> 00:26:52.950
Wait, you one of the rescue workers from the bus, right?

00:26:52.950 --> 00:26:54.950
I thought I recognized you for a guy without a unit.

00:26:54.950 --> 00:26:57.950
for a guy without a uniform, you helped a lot of people.

00:26:57.950 --> 00:26:58.950
Oh, I didn't do anything.

00:26:58.950 --> 00:27:00.950
I mean, you're the real hero.

00:27:00.950 --> 00:27:02.950
You help people for a living.

00:27:02.950 --> 00:27:04.950
I'm Clark Kent.

00:27:04.950 --> 00:27:07.950
Davis Bloom. I met your fiancée.

00:27:07.950 --> 00:27:10.950
Clark, congratulations. She's a real catch.

00:27:10.950 --> 00:27:12.950
I'm getting married?

00:27:12.950 --> 00:27:15.950
Well, I thought that, because I saw you and Chloe together

00:27:15.950 --> 00:27:17.950
and you seem pretty close when she said she was engaged.

00:27:17.950 --> 00:27:18.950
Chloe's engaged?

00:27:18.950 --> 00:27:23.970
Okay, my brain's gone completely D-O-A. Clark.

00:27:23.970 --> 00:27:25.970
She said she hadn't told anyone yet.

00:27:25.970 --> 00:27:27.970
Do me a favor.

00:27:27.970 --> 00:27:29.970
Don't tell her I said anything.

00:27:29.970 --> 00:27:34.400
I won't reveal my source.

00:27:34.400 --> 00:27:45.309
Davis, the paramedic we met on the street, came by with the paperwork.

00:27:45.309 --> 00:27:47.309
His friends want to meet you.

00:27:47.309 --> 00:27:50.309
Change a plan, Chloe. I'm leaving Metropolis.

00:27:50.309 --> 00:27:52.309
Don't you think that you should read this first?

00:27:52.309 --> 00:27:54.309
I mean, this place sounds really great.

00:27:54.309 --> 00:27:55.309
Maybe it is.

00:27:55.309 --> 00:27:56.309
The city's gone sour.

00:27:56.309 --> 00:27:58.309
Like way past its shelf life.

00:27:58.309 --> 00:27:59.309
I have to go.

00:27:59.309 --> 00:28:01.309
Look, I know what happened with Tommy was awful,

00:28:01.309 --> 00:28:04.309
but running away is not the answer.

00:28:04.309 --> 00:28:05.309
Besides,

00:28:05.309 --> 00:28:07.309
It's not safe out there for you by yourself.

00:28:07.309 --> 00:28:09.309
You think the streets are dangerous?

00:28:09.309 --> 00:28:11.309
Try a lock door with someone else holding the key.

00:28:11.309 --> 00:28:12.309
And thanks.

00:28:12.309 --> 00:28:13.309
They're not going to lock you in.

00:28:13.309 --> 00:28:15.309
Look, tell you what, I'll call them for you.

00:28:15.309 --> 00:28:16.309
Chloe, stop.

00:28:16.309 --> 00:28:19.309
I don't need a den mother and I won't go see those people.

00:28:19.309 --> 00:28:20.309
Then they'll come here to see you.

00:28:20.309 --> 00:28:21.309
You're not listening to me.

00:28:21.309 --> 00:28:23.309
I'm just trying to help you back.

00:28:23.309 --> 00:28:31.940
I wish you hadn't made me to you that.

00:28:31.940 --> 00:28:50.650
There's nothing in here about a meteor infection.

00:28:50.650 --> 00:28:52.650
Here, let me take a look.

00:28:52.650 --> 00:28:53.650
Knock yourself out.

00:28:53.650 --> 00:28:55.650
I'm not sure we're on the right track, Lois.

00:28:55.650 --> 00:28:57.650
Tommy's death seems suspicious.

00:28:57.650 --> 00:28:58.650
Of course, suspicious.

00:28:58.650 --> 00:29:01.150
The guy blew himself up just by rubbing his hands together,

00:29:01.150 --> 00:29:02.650
wrinkling his nose, or whatever he did.

00:29:02.650 --> 00:29:04.650
They didn't find any meteor rock in his system,

00:29:04.650 --> 00:29:06.650
but they did find metal shrapnel from the barrels.

00:29:06.650 --> 00:29:08.650
Lois, if Tommy is responsible for the blast

00:29:08.650 --> 00:29:11.650
and the barrels would have blown away from him, not into him, right?

00:29:11.650 --> 00:29:13.650
Don't clear his name just yet, Sherlock.

00:29:13.650 --> 00:29:15.650
The kid was dangerous, a real live wire.

00:29:15.650 --> 00:29:16.650
Check his rap sheet at the back.

00:29:16.650 --> 00:29:18.650
Armed robbery, B&E and carjacking.

00:29:18.650 --> 00:29:21.650
Basically, that firecracker was a major menace to metropolis.

00:29:21.650 --> 00:29:24.650
But there's no mention of explosives in any of these crimes, Lois.

00:29:24.650 --> 00:29:26.650
If you were criminal, with these abilities,

00:29:26.650 --> 00:29:27.650
wouldn't you use them?

00:29:27.650 --> 00:29:30.650
Well, if Tommy didn't kill himself, then who did?

00:29:30.650 --> 00:29:32.650
Beck claimed that Tommy blew up the bus,

00:29:32.650 --> 00:29:36.990
but she was there for both of the blasts.

00:29:36.990 --> 00:29:43.099
Oh my God, my cousin's babysitting psycho spice.

00:29:43.099 --> 00:29:44.099
Clark, what if...

00:29:44.099 --> 00:29:47.220
Come on.

00:29:47.220 --> 00:29:50.500
Believe me, I understand.

00:29:50.500 --> 00:29:54.500
It can be tough to control your powers when you're angry or afraid,

00:29:54.500 --> 00:29:58.500
like on the bus or with Tommy.

00:29:58.500 --> 00:30:00.500
Those weren't accidents.

00:30:00.500 --> 00:30:02.500
I knew what I was doing.

00:30:02.500 --> 00:30:04.500
But there's some bad people chasing.

00:30:04.500 --> 00:30:08.500
me. They cornered me on the bus. I had to fight back.

00:30:08.500 --> 00:30:10.500
So you set up Tommy to take the blame?

00:30:10.500 --> 00:30:15.279
You killed him.

00:30:15.279 --> 00:30:17.279
He helped them find me.

00:30:17.279 --> 00:30:22.279
Three years ago, some corporate types locked me in their private prison.

00:30:22.279 --> 00:30:26.279
It was a nightmare. They ran tests on me every day.

00:30:26.279 --> 00:30:30.279
Last week, something happened, and we were all let go.

00:30:30.279 --> 00:30:33.279
They tagged us on the way out.

00:30:33.279 --> 00:30:36.279
I ran before they could do it to me.

00:30:36.279 --> 00:30:39.279
This place where there are lots of people there with powers?

00:30:39.279 --> 00:30:40.279
Yeah.

00:30:40.279 --> 00:30:42.279
I told Tommy all about it.

00:30:42.279 --> 00:30:44.279
And you know what he did?

00:30:44.279 --> 00:30:46.279
He sold me out.

00:30:46.279 --> 00:30:48.279
He let them straight to me.

00:30:48.279 --> 00:30:50.279
I think that what he deserved.

00:30:50.279 --> 00:30:53.720
The prison was in Montana, wasn't it?

00:30:53.720 --> 00:30:55.720
Black Creek.

00:30:55.720 --> 00:30:57.720
How did you know that?

00:30:57.720 --> 00:31:02.539
Because I was there.

00:31:02.539 --> 00:31:04.539
I had a meteor power too.

00:31:04.539 --> 00:31:06.539
I could heal people.

00:31:06.539 --> 00:31:08.539
I know how awful it was there.

00:31:08.539 --> 00:31:10.539
Then you know I had to do whatever it took to get away.

00:31:10.539 --> 00:31:12.539
they had me backed into a corner.

00:31:12.539 --> 00:31:17.539
No matter what they do, do you bet you don't kill people.

00:31:17.539 --> 00:31:20.539
Sometimes I don't have a choice.

00:31:20.539 --> 00:31:22.539
Chloe, I'm sorry.

00:31:22.539 --> 00:31:25.539
I can't risk you turning on me too.

00:31:25.539 --> 00:31:48.240
Goodbye, Chloe.

00:31:48.240 --> 00:31:55.039
Clerk, stay away from me.

00:31:55.039 --> 00:31:56.039
I'll hurt you.

00:31:56.039 --> 00:31:58.039
No, you won't.

00:31:58.039 --> 00:32:00.039
You're not afraid of me?

00:32:00.039 --> 00:32:01.039
No.

00:32:01.039 --> 00:32:03.039
I just want to help you.

00:32:03.039 --> 00:32:06.420
After everything I've done,

00:32:06.420 --> 00:32:07.420
why would you?

00:32:07.420 --> 00:32:09.420
I want to help a monster like me.

00:32:09.420 --> 00:32:11.420
Because you're not a monster.

00:32:11.420 --> 00:32:13.420
You've just been led down the wrong path.

00:32:13.420 --> 00:32:20.690
Whatever people find out about me, they get afraid and they try to hurt me.

00:32:20.690 --> 00:32:27.180
So I have to lie. I have to hide what I am.

00:32:27.180 --> 00:32:30.180
You don't have to anymore.

00:32:30.180 --> 00:32:31.180
Not for me.

00:32:31.180 --> 00:32:44.640
We all have something we think we need to hide.

00:32:44.640 --> 00:32:52.890
It's hard, but it does get better.

00:32:52.890 --> 00:33:11.410
It's a good thing you called Lois and told her you were okay.

00:33:11.410 --> 00:33:13.410
She was about to call out the National Guard.

00:33:13.410 --> 00:33:17.509
guard.

00:33:17.509 --> 00:33:20.890
Bet almost killed me, Clark.

00:33:20.890 --> 00:33:23.890
Chloe, there's no way you could have known how dangerous she was.

00:33:23.890 --> 00:33:25.890
Her power was hidden.

00:33:25.890 --> 00:33:27.890
Some sort of high-frequency energy blasts.

00:33:27.890 --> 00:33:29.890
She fooled everyone.

00:33:29.890 --> 00:33:31.890
It's because she didn't trust anyone.

00:33:31.890 --> 00:33:33.890
I mean, I was only in that cell for a few weeks.

00:33:33.890 --> 00:33:36.890
I can't imagine being in there for three years.

00:33:36.890 --> 00:33:39.890
Hopefully she'll find the help she needs to Belle Reeve.

00:33:39.890 --> 00:33:45.390
Yeah, I seriously doubt that being locked away in another cell is going to do any good.

00:33:45.390 --> 00:33:48.390
Do you think if you knew her sooner, you could have helped her deal with her power?

00:33:48.390 --> 00:33:49.390
Chloe, sometimes.

00:33:49.390 --> 00:33:52.390
people who need help the most are the ones who push it away the hardest.

00:33:52.390 --> 00:33:55.390
Which is why someone should be talking to them from day one.

00:33:55.390 --> 00:34:04.200
Looking for this?

00:34:04.200 --> 00:34:10.500
I found it downstairs. You must have lost it when that was chasing you.

00:34:10.500 --> 00:34:18.530
Is there anything you want to tell me?

00:34:18.530 --> 00:34:22.530
I was on my way over here this morning.

00:34:22.530 --> 00:34:28.760
How did you find out? Did Jimmy call you?

00:34:28.760 --> 00:34:32.329
It's rule number.

00:34:32.329 --> 00:34:35.329
11. Always protect your source.

00:34:35.329 --> 00:34:40.210
But I would like the whole story.

00:34:40.210 --> 00:34:43.860
How long have you been engaged?

00:34:43.860 --> 00:34:44.860
How long have you been engaged?

00:34:44.860 --> 00:34:47.559
A week.

00:34:47.559 --> 00:34:51.559
I said yes the night I came back from Montana.

00:34:51.559 --> 00:34:56.090
You could have called.

00:34:56.090 --> 00:34:57.090
Any time.

00:34:57.090 --> 00:35:04.599
We've been friends for such a long time.

00:35:04.599 --> 00:35:06.599
We're more than just friends, Chloe.

00:35:06.599 --> 00:35:15.010
When Jimmy and I get married,

00:35:15.010 --> 00:35:18.010
things will probably change.

00:35:18.010 --> 00:35:19.010
Between us.

00:35:19.010 --> 00:35:27.579
I mean, I don't know if I'm ready for that just yet.

00:35:27.579 --> 00:35:35.519
Are you?

00:35:35.519 --> 00:35:37.519
I know that your happiness is one of the most important things

00:35:37.519 --> 00:35:39.519
in the world to me.

00:35:39.519 --> 00:35:40.519
And that you and Jimmy

00:35:40.519 --> 00:35:48.630
you'll have a wonderful life together.

00:35:48.630 --> 00:35:49.630
Don't worry about anything else.

00:35:49.630 --> 00:36:28.719
Hello, Bet.

00:36:28.719 --> 00:36:30.719
You should have died on that bus.

00:36:30.719 --> 00:36:36.539
The last time we met, things did get a little fiery.

00:36:36.539 --> 00:36:38.539
Lucky for me, I ducked.

00:36:38.539 --> 00:36:45.159
They're taking you to Belle Reeve.

00:36:45.159 --> 00:36:48.159
I'm sure after a few years of good behavior,

00:36:48.159 --> 00:36:51.159
they'll let you see the sun again.

00:36:51.159 --> 00:36:53.159
Or you could come with me.

00:36:53.159 --> 00:36:58.159
I'd rather be a prisoner there than you're a lab rat in Montana.

00:36:58.159 --> 00:36:59.159
Go push your cheese.

00:36:59.159 --> 00:37:00.159
somewhere else.

00:37:00.159 --> 00:37:13.110
I didn't build that place, bed.

00:37:13.110 --> 00:37:16.110
And after I heard about all the terrible things happening there,

00:37:16.110 --> 00:37:18.110
I closed it down.

00:37:18.110 --> 00:37:20.110
I tried to tell you.

00:37:20.110 --> 00:37:24.110
If you shut down the Thunderdown, then why are you still coming after me?

00:37:24.110 --> 00:37:27.619
Because you're a very powerful person.

00:37:27.619 --> 00:37:34.719
And I think it's about time the world started treating you accordingly.

00:37:34.719 --> 00:37:38.670
Don't you?

00:37:38.670 --> 00:37:39.670
Listening.

00:37:39.670 --> 00:37:44.670
I want to introduce you to some people like you.

00:37:44.670 --> 00:37:46.670
Like you.

00:37:46.670 --> 00:37:48.670
A sort of team.

00:37:48.670 --> 00:37:50.670
But only if you want.

00:37:50.670 --> 00:37:51.670
A team?

00:37:51.670 --> 00:37:52.670
Take a look at my file.

00:37:52.670 --> 00:37:55.670
Lady, I don't play well with others.

00:37:55.670 --> 00:38:01.210
I think once you meet everyone, you may finally feel like you fit in.

00:38:01.210 --> 00:38:04.210
I remember what it was like to be your age.

00:38:04.210 --> 00:38:09.980
Alone, trapped.

00:38:09.980 --> 00:38:13.619
The injustice of it all.

00:38:13.619 --> 00:38:21.980
I can help.

00:38:21.980 --> 00:38:23.980
The team's only as good as it's weakest link.

00:38:23.980 --> 00:38:28.519
Look what happened to me on the bus.

00:38:28.519 --> 00:38:29.519
Why scat out someone?

00:38:29.519 --> 00:38:31.519
Somebody is just going to choke on their own smoke.

00:38:31.519 --> 00:38:34.519
Don't be so hard on yourself.

00:38:34.519 --> 00:38:42.130
We'll make a hero out of you yet.

00:38:42.130 --> 00:39:02.840
Looking good, Smallville.

00:39:02.840 --> 00:39:05.840
Close make the man who helped me and make the front page.

00:39:05.840 --> 00:39:10.920
I'll try to hold back your journalistic fervor.

00:39:10.920 --> 00:39:13.920
I'm glad you got your story, Lois, but took a few more turns than I would have liked.

00:39:13.920 --> 00:39:16.920
So did you, Houdini. You're there one minute gone the next.

00:39:16.920 --> 00:39:17.920
We're standing next to an elevator.

00:39:17.920 --> 00:39:19.920
I don't know why you had to take the stairs.

00:39:19.920 --> 00:39:21.920
Well, I'm sorry that you can't keep up.

00:39:21.920 --> 00:39:24.920
The important thing is that Chloe figured it out on her own and she's okay.

00:39:24.920 --> 00:39:25.920
she's okay.

00:39:25.920 --> 00:39:26.920
Tell me about it.

00:39:26.920 --> 00:39:29.920
If she hadn't diffused little Miss Landline,

00:39:29.920 --> 00:39:34.199
we'd be fitting her for a coffin instead of a wedding dress.

00:39:34.199 --> 00:39:36.199
When did you hear about the wedding?

00:39:36.199 --> 00:39:38.199
She just called.

00:39:38.199 --> 00:39:40.199
Can't believe my cousin is getting married.

00:39:40.199 --> 00:39:45.460
They're in love, Lois.

00:39:45.460 --> 00:39:47.460
You should be happy for them.

00:39:47.460 --> 00:39:50.460
Well, at least the rest of us have work.

00:39:50.460 --> 00:39:56.030
Here, I finished proofing the obit.

00:39:56.030 --> 00:39:58.030
Well, Lois, don't hold anything back.

00:39:58.030 --> 00:40:00.030
Those aren't notes of discouragement.

00:40:00.030 --> 00:40:01.030
They're notes of encouragement.

00:40:01.030 --> 00:40:03.030
You've got talent, Smallville.

00:40:03.030 --> 00:40:05.030
What?

00:40:05.030 --> 00:40:07.030
Like when I first started out at The Inquisitor,

00:40:07.030 --> 00:40:10.030
all I cared about was getting the best stories on the front page.

00:40:10.030 --> 00:40:13.030
It seems like a dream come true.

00:40:13.030 --> 00:40:16.030
Sure, but sitting here now with you, I think,

00:40:16.030 --> 00:40:20.030
I'm more proud that we uncover the truth than I am over having a headline.

00:40:20.030 --> 00:40:27.179
Thanks for helping me break the story, clerk.

00:40:27.179 --> 00:40:32.989
Keep up the good work.

00:40:32.989 --> 00:40:35.989
You've got a long career ahead of you at The Daily Planet.

00:40:35.989 --> 00:41:16.269
Hi, Davis. It's Chloe Sullivan.

00:41:16.269 --> 00:41:17.269
I, uh...

00:41:17.269 --> 00:41:22.269
I just wanted to call and say thanks for helping out with Bet.

00:41:22.269 --> 00:41:25.269
It's too bad that that didn't work out.

00:41:25.269 --> 00:41:31.269
But I also wanted to let you know that I've decided to reopen the ISIS Foundation.

00:41:31.269 --> 00:41:34.269
And a few things that you said helped me make that decision.

00:41:34.269 --> 00:41:37.269
So, thanks.

00:41:37.269 --> 00:41:38.269
Okay.

00:41:38.269 --> 00:41:41.269
Well, stay safe out there.

00:41:41.269 --> 00:41:42.269
Take care.

